	"title"		"Conveyor Belt Quick Filters"
	"description"		"[b]Stop clicking every icon in the Input Hopper and Filter windows.[/b]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]toggle[/b] button on every category header: turns the whole category on, or off when it is already all on
[*][b]Quick Filters[/b] list beside the window: All, Stone + ore, All farmed, Base materials, All food, Metal bars
[*]Each quick filter is a toggle and leaves every other resource alone
[*]Make your own filters in a text file (see below)
[*]Works in the Input Hopper (while Whitelist allowed resources is on) and in the Filter
[*]Both features can be switched off under Settings - Mods
[*]Uses the game's own icon click, so nothing is patched and saves stay normal
[*]Works while paused, and does nothing in the background
[/list]

[h2]Your own filters[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Open the [url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-quickfilters/blob/main/docs/QuickFilters-defaults.txt]defaults file on GitHub[/url]: it lists the format, every resource id and every category
[*]Create the folder %localappdata%\Whiskerwood\Saved\mods\QuickFiltersConfig
[*]Save a text file named QuickFilters.txt there (not QuickFilters.txt.txt)
[*]Write a [presets] line, then one filter per line, for example: Fuel stuff = coal, fuel, wood
[*]Load your save
[/olist]
Use @ore, @rawFood and so on for a whole category, * for everything. A line with a built-in name replaces that filter; Name = with nothing after it removes it.

[h2]Source[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-quickfilters]GitHub[/url]

Created using the [url=https://github.com/Whiskerwood-Modding/Whiskerwood-Project]Whiskerwood modkit[/url]."
	"changenote"		"1.0: first release."
}
